const e="Navigating Eating Disorder Treatment in Brisbane’s Social Media Age | Michelle Barratt Psychology",a="Finding Safe Eating Disorder Support in a Digital World Eating disorder treatment in Brisbane now has to include real-life and online life. Many of us scroll ",t='<!--$--><section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-plum to-rose text-white"><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20"><div><nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-6"><ol class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-white/75"><li><a class="hover:text-white" href="/">Home</a></li><li aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3 w-3"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg></li><li><a class="hover:text-white active" href="/blog" data-status="active" aria-current="page">Blog</a></li><li aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3 w-3"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg></li><li class="text-white" aria-current="page">Navigating Eating Disorder Treatment in Brisbane’s Social Media Age</li></ol></nav><p class="text-[12px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-white/85 mb-3">8 May 2026</p><h1 class="text-white text-[32px] md:text-[44px] font-semibold leading-[1.08] max-w-3xl">Navigating Eating Disorder Treatment in Brisbane’s Social Media Age</h1><div class="h-[3px] w-16 bg-sun my-5" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="max-w-2xl text-[16px] md:text-[17px] text-white/95 space-y-3"><p>Finding Safe Eating Disorder Support in a Digital World Eating disorder treatment in Brisbane now has to include real-life and online life. Many of us scroll through feeds filled with bodies, food hacks, fitness challenges and wellness tren</p></div><div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 bg-white text-plum hover:bg-blush " href="/contact">Contact Us</a></div></div></div></section><section class="bg-soft !py-0"><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="py-14 md:py-16"><img src="https://michellebarrattpsychology.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/getty-images-KUYyJYtvy3s-unsplash.jpg" alt="" class="w-full aspect-[16/9] max-h-[520px] object-cover rounded border border-lilac"/></div></div></section><section class="bg-white "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">Finding Safe Eating Disorder Support in a Digital World</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Eating disorder treatment in Brisbane now has to include real-life and online life. Many of us scroll through feeds filled with bodies, food hacks, fitness challenges and wellness trends before we even get out of bed. For someone who already feels worried about food or how they look, this can quietly make things worse.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Around times of change, like going back to uni, training for winter sport or spending more time indoors when the weather cools, it can be even harder to block out these messages. Diet plans, challenges and “before and after” photos can seem normal, even when they are actually very risky. Safe support needs to look at what is happening on your plate, in your body and on your phone.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">At Michelle Barratt Psychology, we work with children, teens, adults, couples and families across Brisbane and Queensland. We offer in-clinic sessions in Toowong and Wynnum West, and telehealth for those who are further away or need more flexibility. Our focus is to blend evidence-based eating disorder treatment with practical help for managing life online.</p></div></section><section class="bg-soft "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">How Social Media Shapes Body Image and Eating Behaviours</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Social media is designed to keep attention, not to protect mental health. The more time you spend looking at certain content, the more similar posts and videos you are likely to see. This can make unsafe ideas seem normal.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Common online triggers include comparison culture (constantly checking your body against friends, influencers or athletes), edited and filtered photos that make it hard to know what “real” bodies look like, fitness and diet influencers who present strict routines as “discipline” or “self-care,” and “clean eating” and wellness trends that quietly cut out more and more foods.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">In Brisbane, young people also face a mix of pressures that can intensify these messages. This can include school and uni stress (including comments about weight or fitness in peer groups), sport and dance settings that focus heavily on performance and appearance, and social events where photos are shared widely and quickly.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">It is normal to have days when you do not feel great about your body. That is different from an eating disorder. Signs that things may have moved into eating disorder territory can include:</p><ul class="max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6"><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Extreme dieting, skipping meals or cutting out whole food groups without medical advice</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Rigid food rules, such as only eating at certain times or being very distressed if plans change</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Secretive eating or lying about what has been eaten</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Compensatory behaviour after eating, such as forced exercise or other harmful actions</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Mood swings, sleep problems, or strong anxiety linked to food or body image</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Pulling away from friends, activities or family meals</span></li></ul><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">If you notice a mix of these signs in yourself or someone you care about, an early assessment with a clinical psychologist or another qualified health professional is very important.</p></div></section><section class="bg-white "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">What Effective Eating Disorder Treatment Looks Like Today</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Good eating disorder treatment in Brisbane usually starts with a thorough assessment. This includes understanding current eating patterns, thoughts about weight and shape, medical safety, mood, anxiety and what is happening at school, work and home. From there, a clear diagnosis and plan can be made.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Treatment often includes:</p><ul class="max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6"><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Clear goals around physical health, eating patterns and daily functioning</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>A collaborative plan that you understand and agree to</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Regular reviews to track progress and adjust support as needed</span></li></ul><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">At Michelle Barratt Psychology, our team draws on different evidence-based approaches, explained in simple language and tailored to each person’s age and needs. These may include Family-Based Treatment (FBT) for children and adolescents, where parents play an active role in supporting meals and weight restoration, and Enhanced Cognitive Behaviour Therapy (CBT-E), which focuses on unhelpful thoughts and behaviours around food, weight and shape, and building regular, flexible eating. We also use other therapies to address anxiety, mood, trauma, perfectionism or self-worth concerns that sit alongside the eating disorder.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">A multidisciplinary team is often important. Alongside psychological treatment, people may need support from:</p><ul class="max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6"><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>A GP to monitor physical health and coordinate care</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>A dietitian with experience in eating disorders</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>A psychiatrist, where medication or higher-level care is needed</span></li></ul><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Plans are shaped around school timetables, work rosters, family life and travel across Brisbane, so treatment can be consistent and sustainable.</p></div></section><section class="bg-soft "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">Caring for Children and Teens in a Hyper-Connected Era</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Parents and carers are often the first to notice small changes. Warning signs in children and teens can look like:</p><ul class="max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6"><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Avoiding family meals or claiming to have already eaten</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Cutting food into tiny pieces, eating very slowly or being very focused on ingredients</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>A sudden interest in “healthy” recipes, weight loss content or fitness accounts</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Changes in mood, becoming more irritable, flat or anxious</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Drop in school engagement, tiredness, or pulling away from friends and hobbies</span></li></ul><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">If you are worried, it can help to:</p><ul class="max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6"><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Stay calm and open, rather than accusing or blaming</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Ask gentle questions about how they are feeling, not just what they are eating</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Show interest in their online world and who they follow</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Set age-appropriate limits on social media use, especially around meals and bedtime</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Arrange a professional assessment instead of waiting to “see if it passes”</span></li></ul><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">At Michelle Barratt Psychology, we work closely with families and aim to make sure support is practical and sustainable at home. Depending on the young person’s age and needs, this may include involving parents or carers in sessions, supporting siblings to understand what is happening in a safe way, and using telehealth for families balancing school, sport and work across Queensland.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">The goal is to give adults clear roles and tools so they do not feel alone in a very stressful situation.</p></div></section><section class="bg-white "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">Adults, Social Media Pressures and Recovery in Real Life</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Eating disorders are not just a teenage issue. Many adults manage careers, study, parenting and relationships while hiding intense struggles with food and body image. Social media can add pressure in different ways for adults, such as:</p><ul class="max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6"><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Wellness content that labels some foods as “toxic” or “guilty”</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Constant diet trends that promise quick fixes</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Fitness trackers that turn movement into numbers and “streaks”</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Messages about “getting your body back” after pregnancy or other life changes</span></li></ul><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">For adults, treatment often includes practical strategies like identifying personal triggers online and offline, challenging rigid rules around food, movement and rest, learning to notice and respond differently to guilt, shame or anxiety, building supportive routines around meals, sleep and social connection, and involving partners or close supports where helpful. We also help adults think about how their digital habits fit with their values, not just their fears.</p></div></section><section class="bg-soft "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">Using Technology to Support, Not Sabotage, Recovery</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Phones and apps are not all harmful. Used with care, they can actually support treatment. Useful options can include:</p><ul class="max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6"><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Telehealth appointments when travel is hard, or you live outside central Brisbane</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Secure messaging and reminders to help keep track of tasks set in therapy</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Symptom or mood tracking tools that you review together with your clinician</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Curated, recovery-focused content that gently challenges toxic online messages</span></li></ul><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Clinicians at Michelle Barratt Psychology can work with you to set realistic time limits around social media, choose accounts that support body respect, diversity and mental health, question unhelpful beliefs (such as “I must look like that to be worthy”), and build offline activities, friendships, and coping skills so online life is only one part of your world.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Flexible in-clinic sessions in Toowong and Wynnum West, combined with telehealth across Queensland, mean treatment can be fitted around school, uni, work and seasonal changes in routine. Our focus is always on compassionate, evidence-based care that respects the real pressures people face, both on screen and off.</p></div></section><section class="bg-white "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">Take The First Step Toward Eating Disorder Recovery Today</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">If you or someone you care about is struggling with food, body image or exercise, we are here to support you with evidence-based, compassionate care. At Michelle Barratt Psychology, our eating disorder treatment in Brisbane is tailored to your unique needs so you can work toward lasting change at a pace that feels manageable. Reach out to contact us, and we will help you find a starting point that feels safe, respectful and focused on your wellbeing.</p></div></section><section class="bg-blush "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold mb-8">More articles</h2><div class="grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3"><a class="group bg-white rounded overflow-hidden border border-lilac flex flex-col transition-shadow duration-300 hover:shadow-lg" href="/blog/recognising-ptsd-counselling-needs"><div class="aspect-[3/2] bg-lilac overflow-hidden"><img src="https://michellebarrattpsychology.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/recognising-ptsd-counselling-needs-featured.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105"/></div><div class="p-6 flex flex-col flex-1"><p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-rose mb-2">23 October 2026</p><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold leading-snug">Recognising PTSD Counselling Needs in Toowong Adults</h3><p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/80 line-clamp-3">Post-traumatic stress disorder, or PTSD, is not only something that happens to people in movies or in extreme situations. It can grow quietly in everyday lif…</p><span class="mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ocean">Read article<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right h-4 w-4" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></span></div></a><a class="group bg-white rounded overflow-hidden border border-lilac flex flex-col transition-shadow duration-300 hover:shadow-lg" href="/blog/online-therapy-in-brisbane-when-you"><div class="aspect-[3/2] bg-lilac overflow-hidden"><img src="https://michellebarrattpsychology.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/online-therapy-in-brisbane-when-you-featured.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105"/></div><div class="p-6 flex flex-col flex-1"><p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-rose mb-2">16 October 2026</p><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold leading-snug">Online Therapy in Brisbane When You Can’t Find Local Support</h3><p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/80 line-clamp-3">Trying to find a psychologist in Brisbane can feel exhausting. You search, you join waitlists, you juggle your calendar, and still there is no appointment th…</p><span class="mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ocean">Read article<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right h-4 w-4" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></span></div></a><a class="group bg-white rounded overflow-hidden border border-lilac flex flex-col transition-shadow duration-300 hover:shadow-lg" href="/blog/recognising-trauma-counselling-needs"><div class="aspect-[3/2] bg-lilac overflow-hidden"><img src="https://michellebarrattpsychology.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/recognising-trauma-counselling-needs-featured.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105"/></div><div class="p-6 flex flex-col flex-1"><p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-rose mb-2">9 October 2026</p><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold leading-snug">Recognising Trauma Counselling Needs in Toowong Professionals</h3><p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/80 line-clamp-3">High-performing professionals in Toowong are often good at holding it together. Work is busy, the pressure is high, and most people tell themselves it is jus…</p><span class="mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ocean">Read article<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right h-4 w-4" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></span></div></a></div></div></section><section class="bg-blush"><div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-14 md:py-16 text-center"><p class="text-[12px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-rose mb-2.5">Take the first step</p><h2 class="text-[30px] md:text-[40px] font-semibold leading-[1.1]">Ready to Take the First Step?</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-4 mx-auto" aria-hidden="true"></div><p class="mt-5 text-[17px]">Seeking support can feel overwhelming, but you do not have to navigate life&#x27;s challenges alone. Our administration team can help answer your questions, explain appointment options and connect you with a suitable practitioner.</p><p class="mt-3">Prefer to call? Phone our administration team on <a class="text-ocean underline underline-offset-4 font-medium" href="tel:0731850040">07 3185 0040</a>.</p><div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3"><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 bg-rose text-white hover:bg-[#9d2a59] " href="/practitioners">Book Online</a><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 bg-ocean text-white hover:bg-[#095a6f] " href="/contact">Contact Us</a><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 border border-plum text-plum hover:bg-lilac " href="/therapy-services">Explore Services</a></div><p class="mt-5 text-sm text-ink/70">If in crisis, please call 000.</p></div></section><!--/$-->',s={title:e,description:a,html:t};export{s as default,a as description,t as html,e as title};
